================================================================================
                        CORTANA BOT — INSTALLATION & USER GUIDE
                        For ElDewrito 0.7.1 Dedicated Servers
================================================================================

OVERVIEW
--------
Cortana is an AI-powered chat assistant for ElDewrito servers. Players can ask
questions in game chat and receive real-time responses. The bot also features
server moderation tools, web search, YouTube link fetching, kill streak
announcements, and player join detection.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 1 — REQUIREMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before installing, make sure you have the following:

  - Windows PC running ElDewrito 0.7.1
  - ElDewrito dedicated server files (dedicated_server.bat)
  - Python 3.10 or newer
  - A free Groq API key (primary AI provider)
  - Optional: Cerebras and/or Mistral API keys (fallback providers)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 2 — FOLDER STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Create a folder anywhere on your PC for the bot. For example:

  C:\CortanaBot\

Place the following files inside that folder:

  C:\CortanaBot\
      cortana_bot.py      <- the main bot script
      config.txt          <- your settings and API keys
      bans.json           <- created automatically when first ban is issued

Keep all three files in the same folder at all times.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 3 — INSTALLING PYTHON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Go to https://python.org/downloads
2. Download the latest Python version
3. Run the installer
4. IMPORTANT: Check the box that says "Add Python to PATH" before installing
5. Complete the installation

To verify Python installed correctly, open Command Prompt and run:

  python --version

You should see something like: Python 3.12.x

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 4 — INSTALLING REQUIRED LIBRARIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Open Command Prompt and run this command:

  pip install websocket-client requests duckduckgo-search

Wait for it to finish. You only need to do this once.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 5 — GETTING API KEYS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You need at least one API key to run the bot. Groq is recommended as the
primary provider since it is free and fast.

  GROQ (Primary — Recommended)
  -----------------------------
  1. Go to https://console.groq.com
  2. Sign up for a free account
  3. Click "API Keys" in the left sidebar
  4. Click "Create Key" and give it a name (e.g. "cortana-bot")
  5. Copy the key — it starts with gsk_

  CEREBRAS (Optional Fallback)
  -----------------------------
  1. Go to https://cloud.cerebras.ai
  2. Sign up for a free account
  3. Navigate to API Keys and create one
  4. Copy the key

  MISTRAL (Optional Fallback — 1B tokens/month free)
  ---------------------------------------------------
  1. Go to https://console.mistral.ai
  2. Sign up for a free account
  3. Navigate to API Keys and create one
  4. Copy the key

You only need Groq to get started. Cerebras and Mistral are optional backups
that activate automatically if Groq hits its rate limit.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 6 — CONFIGURING THE BOT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Open config.txt in Notepad and fill in your values:

  GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_yourkeyhere
  CEREBRAS_API_KEY=yourkeyhere
  MISTRAL_API_KEY=yourkeyhere
  RCON_PASSWORD=yourserverpassword
  RCON_PORT=11776
  OWNER_UUID=youruuidhere

Notes:
  - Leave CEREBRAS_API_KEY and MISTRAL_API_KEY blank if you don't have them
  - RCON_PASSWORD must match Server.RconPassword in dewrito_prefs.cfg
  - RCON_PORT is almost always 11776 for dedicated servers
  - OWNER_UUID is your player UUID — see Section 7 for how to find it

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 7 — FINDING YOUR PLAYER UUID
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Your UUID is a unique identifier tied to your ElDewrito account. It is used
to verify that only you can use admin commands.

To find your UUID:
  1. Start your ElDewrito dedicated server
  2. Join the server as a player
  3. Open your browser and go to: http://localhost:11775
  4. Find your player entry in the JSON output
  5. Copy the value of the "uid" field (e.g. "a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8")

Paste that value into config.txt next to OWNER_UUID.
Do not include the "0x" prefix if it appears.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 8 — CONFIGURING ELDEWRITO FOR RCON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The bot communicates with your server via RCON. You need to enable it.

1. Find your dewrito_prefs.cfg file. It is usually located at:
     C:\Users\YourName\AppData\Local\ElDewrito\

   Or in your ElDewrito game folder.

2. Open it in Notepad and add or edit these lines:

     Server.RconPassword "yourpassword"
     Server.SendChatToRconClients "1"

3. The password here must match RCON_PASSWORD in config.txt exactly.

4. Save the file and restart the dedicated server.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 9 — RUNNING THE BOT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

IMPORTANT: Always start the dedicated server BEFORE running the bot.

Step 1: Start the dedicated server
  - Double-click dedicated_server.bat in your ElDewrito folder
  - Wait for it to finish loading (you will see "starting game..." message)

Step 2: Run the bot
  - Open Command Prompt
  - Navigate to your bot folder:
      cd C:\CortanaBot
  - Run the bot:
      python cortana_bot.py

Step 3: Verify it is working
  - You should see:
      [RCON] Connected and authenticated!
      [LOG] Ready.
  - In-game you will see:
      Cortana: Cortana online. Type @cortana <question> to get started.

Leave the Command Prompt window open while the server is running.
Closing it will stop the bot.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 10 — PLAYER COMMANDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Any player on the server can use these commands in game chat:

  @cortana <question>     Ask Cortana anything
  @ai <question>          Same as @cortana
  !ai <question>          Same as @cortana
  /ai <question>          Same as @cortana
  @bot <question>         Same as @cortana

Examples:
  @cortana what is the best weapon in Halo 3?
  @ai find me the Halo theme on YouTube
  @cortana who is winning right now?
  @ai search for ElDewrito download

The bot has a 30-second cooldown per player to prevent spam.
If the bot is busy, it will tell you to try again shortly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 11 — ADMIN COMMANDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These commands can only be used by the server owner (verified by UUID).
If anyone else tries to use them, the bot will deny access.

  BOT CONTROL
  -----------
  !ai on                  Turn the bot on
  !ai off                 Turn the bot off
  !ai status              Show current status, provider, cooldown, queue info
  !ai clear               Reset all player cooldowns immediately
  !ai cooldown <seconds>  Change the per-player cooldown
                          Example: !ai cooldown 60

  MODERATION
  ----------
  !ai kick <name>                 Kick a player from the server
                                  Example: !ai kick PlayerName

  !ai ban <name>                  Permanently ban a player
                                  The player is kicked immediately
                                  Ban is saved to bans.json with name, UUID,
                                  IP address, and date/time
                                  Example: !ai ban PlayerName

  !ai tempban <name> <minutes>    Temporarily ban a player
                                  Player is kicked immediately and cannot
                                  rejoin until the time expires
                                  Example: !ai tempban PlayerName 30

  !ai unban <name>                Remove a ban (permanent or temporary)
                                  Example: !ai unban PlayerName

  !ai banlist                     Show all currently active bans (up to 5)

  AI PROVIDER
  -----------
  !ai provider groq               Force the bot to use Groq
  !ai provider cerebras           Force the bot to use Cerebras
  !ai provider mistral            Force the bot to use Mistral
  !ai provider auto               Return to automatic fallback mode
                                  (Groq → Cerebras → Mistral)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 12 — AUTOMATIC FEATURES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These run automatically without any commands needed:

  KILL STREAK ANNOUNCEMENTS
    Cortana announces kill streaks in chat at milestones:
      5 kills  — "PlayerName is on a killing spree. Impressive, I suppose."
      10 kills — "PlayerName with 10 kills straight. Someone's having a good day."
      15 kills — "PlayerName at 15. At this point I'd recommend the others
                  reconsider their strategy."
      20 kills — "PlayerName is unstoppable. Statistically speaking, anyway."

  PLAYER JOIN GREETING
    When a new player joins the server, Cortana greets them:
      "Welcome, PlayerName. Type @cortana <question> if you need anything."

  BAN ENFORCEMENT
    The bot checks every 10 seconds for banned players who may have joined.
    If a banned player is detected, they are kicked automatically.
    Expired temporary bans are cleaned up automatically.

  AI PROVIDER FALLBACK
    If the primary provider (Groq) fails or hits its rate limit, the bot
    automatically tries Cerebras, then Mistral, without interrupting service.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 13 — BAN LIST FILE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bans are stored in bans.json in the same folder as the script.
The file is created automatically when the first ban is issued.

Each ban entry contains:
  - Player name
  - Player UUID
  - Player IP address
  - Reason for ban
  - Date and time of ban
  - Expiry date/time (for temporary bans) or "permanent"

You can edit this file manually in Notepad if needed, but be careful with
the JSON formatting. Back it up before editing.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 14 — TROUBLESHOOTING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bot says "Connection refused":
  → Make sure the dedicated server is running before starting the bot
  → Make sure you are running the dedicated server, not a listen server
  → Try running eldorado.exe as administrator

Bot connects but chat messages don't appear in game:
  → Make sure Server.SendChatToRconClients "1" is in dewrito_prefs.cfg
  → Restart the dedicated server after editing the cfg file

Bot responds but admin commands don't work:
  → Check that OWNER_UUID in config.txt matches your actual UUID exactly
  → Find your UUID at http://localhost:11775 while in the server

API errors in Command Prompt:
  → Check that your API key in config.txt is correct and has no extra spaces
  → If Groq is rate limited, it will automatically try the next provider

Password authentication fails:
  → Make sure RCON_PASSWORD in config.txt matches Server.RconPassword in
    dewrito_prefs.cfg exactly, including capitalization

Bot stops responding after a while:
  → The RCON connection may have dropped — restart the bot script

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 15 — UPDATING API KEYS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To update or add API keys at any time:
  1. Open config.txt in Notepad
  2. Edit the relevant line
  3. Save the file
  4. Restart the bot (Ctrl+C to stop, then python cortana_bot.py again)

You do not need to modify the script itself for any key changes.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 16 — MOVING THE BOT TO A NEW PC
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To move the bot to a different computer:
  1. Install Python on the new PC (Section 3)
  2. Install the required libraries (Section 4)
  3. Copy the entire CortanaBot folder to the new PC
  4. Update config.txt with the new server's RCON password if different
  5. Run as normal

The bans.json file will carry over with all existing bans intact.

